Explaination of the comand 
    
"start": "IS_TS_NODE=true ts-node -r tsconfig-paths/register -r ts-node/register dist/main",

IS_TS_NODE=true
This sets an environment variable.

if (process.env.IS_TS_NODE === 'true') {
  // Do something only in ts-node mode
}

ts-node
This is a tool that runs TypeScript files without compiling them into .js first.
Think of it like node, but for .ts files.

-r tsconfig-paths/register
-r means "require this module before running".

tsconfig-paths 
allows support for path aliases (like @app/, @module/) defined in tsconfig.json.
For example, this in tsconfig.json:
"paths": {
  "@user/*": ["src/user/*"]
}
will work correctly when this register is used.


